From: Anland Hyprland Maintainers
Date: Fri, 8 Aug 2026 10:10:00 +0800
Subject: fix: remove ANR data by its associated window

The close-event cleanup accidentally compares an SANRData smart pointer to a
window smart pointer. That is invalid with current hyprutils and cannot have
been the intended association test. Reuse fitsWindow(), which identifies the
ANR record associated with the closing window.

---
 src/managers/ANRManager.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/src/managers/ANRManager.cpp
+++ b/src/managers/ANRManager.cpp
@@ -52,7 +52,7 @@ CANRManager::CANRManager() {
             d->dialogSaidWait  = false;
         }
 
-        std::erase_if(m_data, [&window](auto& w) { return w == window; });
+        std::erase_if(m_data, [&window](const auto& data) { return data->fitsWindow(window); });
     });
 
     m_timer->updateTimeout(TIMER_TIMEOUT);
